	<div id="container-1ccfb671a5" class="bcl-container  bcl-container--bg-white bcl-container--pt-sm bcl-container--pb-none   " tabindex="-1" data-component="bcl-container">
		
		<div class="sectionheading"><div data-cmp-is="bcl-sectionheading" class="bcl-sectionheading margin-bottom-none bcl-sectionheading__medium-sb">
	

	<div class="bcl-sectionheading__title">
<div class="bcl-title " id="title-7263ae9784" data-component="bcl-title">
    
        <h2 class="bcl-title__text bcl-title--align-left bcl-typography bcl-typography--heading-xl" itemprop="headline" data-context="bcl-title">
            
                Mitigation with Akamai App &amp; API Protector
            
            
        </h2>
    
</div>


    



</div>

    
<div data-cmp-is="text" class="bcl-text   " data-component="bcl-text" data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;text-c071c99d05&#34;:{&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;akamai/components/brand-cl/text&#34;,&#34;repo:modifyDate&#34;:&#34;2026-10-21T14:29:16Z&#34;,&#34;xdm:text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>Akamai App &amp;amp; API Protector customers are protected because we have released security updates to address this CVE and monitor for exploitation attempts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>&lt;ul>\r\n&lt;li>&lt;b>Adaptive Security Engine&lt;/b>: 3000991 v1 — &lt;b data-rte-class=\&#34;rte-temp\&#34;>&lt;b data-rte-class=\&#34;rte-temp\&#34;>&lt;b data-rte-class=\&#34;rte-temp\&#34;>&lt;span class=\&#34;code\&#34;>PHP Remote Code Execution Attack Detected (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619&lt;/span>&lt;/b>&lt;/b>&lt;/b>)&lt;/li>\r\n&lt;/ul>\r\n&lt;p>Based on our investigation, Akamai App &amp;amp; API Protector is mitigating weaponized payloads with existing command injection rules.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>\r\n&lt;/p>\r\n&lt;p>The most effective defense continues to be the prompt application of vendor patches. For organizations that cannot patch immediately, applying web application firewall rules is critical to block attack attempts.&lt;/p>\r\n&#34;}}">
     
   
    <p>Akamai App &amp; API Protector customers are protected because we have released security updates to address this CVE and monitor for exploitation attempts. </p>
<p></p><ul><li><b>Adaptive Security Engine</b>: 3000991 v1 — <b data-rte-class="rte-temp"><b data-rte-class="rte-temp"><b data-rte-class="rte-temp"><span class="code">PHP Remote Code Execution Attack Detected (CVE-2026-109618, CVE-2026-109619</span></b></b></b>)</li></ul>
<p>Based on our investigation, Akamai App &amp; API Protector is mitigating weaponized payloads with existing command injection rules. </p>

<p>The most effective defense continues to be the prompt application of vendor patches. For organizations that cannot patch immediately, applying web application firewall rules is critical to block attack attempts.</p>

       
    
       
</div>

    




	
</div>


</div>

		
	</div>

</div>
<div class="container responsivegrid">

    
	
	<div id="container-8d49f7ae4c" class="bcl-container  bcl-container--bg-white bcl-container--pt-sm bcl-container--pb-none   " tabindex="-1" data-component="bcl-container">
		
		<div class="sectionheading"><div data-cmp-is="bcl-sectionheading" class="bcl-sectionheading margin-bottom-none bcl-sectionheading__medium-sb">
	

	<div class="bcl-sectionheading__title">
<div class="bcl-title " id="title-a89af3004c" data-component="bcl-title">
    
        <h2 class="bcl-title__text bcl-title--align-left bcl-typography bcl-typography--heading-sm-semibold" itemprop="headline" data-context="bcl-title">
            
                Stay tuned
            
            
        </h2>
    
</div>


    



</div>

    
<div data-cmp-is="text" class="bcl-text   " data-component="bcl-text" data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;text-b28c9d2cee&#34;:{&#34;@type&#34;:&#34;akamai/components/brand-cl/text&#34;,&#34;repo:modifyDate&#34;:&#34;2026-10-21T12:55:09Z&#34;,&#34;xdm:text&#34;:&#34;&lt;p>The Akamai Security Intelligence Group will continue to monitor, report on, and create mitigations for threats such as these for both our customers and the security community at large. To keep up with more breaking news from the Akamai Security Intelligence Group, check out our &lt;a href=\&#34;/content/akamai/en/security-research.html\&#34; target=\&#34;_self\&#34;>research home page&lt;/a> and follow us on &lt;a href=\&#34;https://x.com/akamai_research\&#34; target=\&#34;_blank\&#34;>social media&lt;/a>.&lt;/p>\r\n&#34;}}">
     
   
    <p>The Akamai Security Intelligence Group will continue to monitor, report on, and create mitigations for threats such as these for both our customers and the security community at large. To keep up with more breaking news from the Akamai Security Intelligence Group, check out our <a href="/security-research" target="_self" rel="noopener noreferrer">research home page</a> and follow us on <a href="https://x.com/akamai_research" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">social media</a>.</p>

       
    
       
</div>

    




	
</div>


</div>

		
	</div>

</div>
